: 2.38 nm), and MM‐PBSA analysis revealed favorable binding free energy (−18.39 kJ/mol), driven predominantly by van der Waals interactions (−184.38 kJ/mol). ADMET profiling predicted excellent intestinal absorption (94.34%) with no AMES toxicity. This study presents a benzothiadiazole derivative as a promising SERT‐modulating lead for AD, establishing a robust computational foundation for experimental validation.
